  "id": "Compound::DB00435 - Gene::2982",
  "verbalization": "Nitric Oxide is implicated in the regulation of vascular tone through its role in vasodilation, which is a shared pathway with Nitroglycerin and Isosorbide Dinitrate. Both Nitric Oxide and Nitroglycerin are known to activate Gucy1a3, a G protein-coupled receptor involved in smooth muscle relaxation. The lowest common ancestor of these entities is the Nitrogen Molecular Entity, suggesting a common biochemical pathway. The integration of these pathways implies that Nitric Oxide and its analogs, such as Nitroglycerin and Isosorbide Dinitrate, share a mechanism of action through Gucy1a3, likely via the production of nitric oxide-derived signaling molecules. This relationship is supported by the presence of a shared pathway and the binding of these compounds to Gucy1a3, highlighting a potential role in vascular regulation.",
